            <ArticleTitle>Clinical experiences of using a cellulose dressing on burns and donor site wounds.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>These preliminary results suggest this temporary skin substitute reduces pain and achieves comparable healing rates to other dressings. Furthermore, its transparency enables regular inspection of the wound bed for signs of infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
